// Contracts known to hold non-zero unshielded token balances on this environment's
// chain, for the unshieldedBalances regression tests (midnightntwrk/midnight-indexer#1245,
// getTokenHoldingContracts). Generated by qa/tools/block-scanner: contract addresses
// discovered in the block scan are queried via contractAction, most recently active
// first, and up to 5 contracts with a positive balance are listed. The token type is the
// contract's largest custom (non-NIGHT) balance, or its NIGHT balance when it holds no
// custom token.
//
// Balances are point-in-time: a contract can spend its tokens after the scan.
//
// The balances are read from the indexer, so the scanned indexer must carry the #1246
// fix and repaired history (backfill or reindex). When no holder is found the file is
// left untouched, since an empty result cannot be told apart from the #1245 regression.
//
// NOTE: contract addresses do NOT survive a chain reset. When a reset makes this file
// stale, re-run the scanner (bun run generate:data) to refresh it.
